<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 0.5px 1px 1px" border-radius="5px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="5px" padding="0px">
    
    <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2
    style="
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin-top: 2px !important;
      margin: 0;
    "
  >
    Rapper turned politician
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    
    
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Summary: Nepal voters back outsider party, reshaping politics and challenging traditional leadership.</strong></p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What happened? </strong>Nepal’s parliamentary elections have produced a major political upset, with the Rastriya Swatantra Party (RSP) emerging as the dominant force. The relatively young party, led by former rapper and Kathmandu mayor Balendra “Balen” Shah, is <a href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/world-news/nepal-election-result-a-new-nepali-party-rsp-led-by-an-ex-rapper-is-set-for-a-landslide-win-in-parliamentary-election/articleshow/129303550.cms" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">projected to secure a landslide victory</a> in parliament. Early results show the party clinching a large share of directly elected seats and leading in several others.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Why?</strong> The surge in support reflects growing frustration among Nepali voters with traditional political parties. Citizens blamed older leaders for corruption, political instability, slow economic growth, and poor governance. Youth voters were drawn to Balendra “Balen” Shah’s outsider image and reform-oriented message, which promised transparency, accountability, and generational change in politics. Shah’s popularity as Kathmandu’s mayor also strengthened his credibility.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Big picture:</strong> The election result signals a potential turning point in Nepal’s political landscape. If the leadership delivers on promises of transparency and governance reforms, it could reshape how politics functions in the country. Regionally, Nepal’s political direction also matters because it sits strategically between India and China, both of which closely watch developments in Kathmandu.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="10px" />
    </mj-section>
