          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇪🇸 Spain - Amnesty plans.</strong> Spain’s government has announced a plan to grant judicial status to at least 500,000 undocumented migrants through a temporary regularisation programme. Eligible migrants who can prove they have lived in Spain for at least five months and have no criminal record will be able to apply for a one-year renewable residency visa between April and June (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crk8rdz5131o" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">Spain shows the way</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇨🇭 Switzerland - Rejects license fee cut.</strong> Swiss voters have rejected a referendum proposal to significantly reduce the annual licence fee that funds the national public broadcaster. The initiative, backed by the right-wing Swiss People’s Party, sought to cut the fee from 335 Swiss francs to 200 francs and exempt more businesses from paying it. In a separate vote, citizens supported a proposal to constitutionally assure the availability of cash (<a href="https://sg.news.yahoo.com/swiss-reject-wing-plan-cut-131259908.html" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">hard rejection</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇹🇷 Turkey - Mayor corruption hearing.</strong> Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu has gone to a hearing alongside more than 400 defendants in a sweeping corruption case. Prosecutors accuse Imamoglu of leading a criminal organization involved in bid-rigging, bribery, and monetary misconduct dating back to his tenure as mayor of Beylikduzu. The 3,900-page indictment includes 142 charges and could result in a prison sentence exceeding 2,000 years if he is convicted (<a href="https://apnews.com/article/turkey-istanbul-mayor-trial-corruption-case-0aeb13e0e6f54e334eb6366ee2189cfa" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">all eyes on this</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇦🇺 Australia - Bondi gunman’s demand. </strong>Naveed Akram, the alleged gunman behind the Bondi Beach shooting, has asked a Sydney court to block media from publishing details about his immediate family due to safety concerns. Akram faces 59 charges, including 15 counts of murder, over the attack at a Jewish festival, considered Australia’s deadliest mass shooting since 1996 (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy8lwnyj40eo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">its personal</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
